{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/698331-kindred-dueling-taunt","id":698331,"title":"Kindred Dueling - Taunt","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-11T20:40:15-07:00","id":698331,"title":"Kindred Dueling - Taunt","content":"So... while most of Kindred Dueling is pretty nifty, I'm struggling to think of a situation where I would ever want to make my enemy even more powerful in a fight rather than less.<br /> <br /> As much as I hate making a thread for such a simple question, perhaps someone can point out something I missed? Why would you ever deliberately make your foe frenzy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T20:56:57-07:00","id":698359,"title":"","content":"Perhaps to make the foe predictable? Perhaps to force a non combat focused vampire to engage you in combat rather than disciplines or some other trickery (like obfuscate). I forget if you can even use disciplines in Frenzy. Particularly non combat ones. To force a stolid opponent to engage you in battle. Is there any shame in frenzying during a duel? In an observed duel frenzying against a composed opponent might seem weak or otherwise lose face for the frenzied vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm asking questions because I'm with you. I'm not sure how useful it is exactly. But those are some thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 10-12-2015, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T21:02:59-07:00","id":698362,"title":"","content":"If you're already more powerful than your opponent their frenzying might be better than their carefully considered attacks. You might need them to do something rash, like break the Masquerade or lash out at someone else you can put between you and the opponent. Plus generally, as far as I can tell, when a vampire frenzies it's sort of a faux pas, especially if said vampire is normally known for their self control.<br /> <br /> Not everyone you duel is going to be a Blood Potency 10 Gangrel with Claws of the Unholy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-12-2015, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T22:48:55-07:00","id":698410,"title":"","content":"Frenzying in front of the whole of Elysium could be considered political suicide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T09:28:37-07:00","id":698657,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I figure the main use of Taunt is to goad your opponent into embarrassing themselves. You might even set the terms of the duel that you lose if you fall to Frenzy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T18:52:24-07:00","id":699263,"title":"","content":"Seems like I didn't miss anything obvious. It seems to be the most situational maneuver of the Style, certainly. Thank you for your input, everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}